{"episodes":{"167281":"Thunderstorms produce a brief tornado in Hardee County and damaging hail up to the size of golf balls in parts of Highlands County.","168290":"Thunderstorms developed along a slow moving cold front on the evening of Monday, April 4, aided by the arrival of an upper level disturbance. All modes of severe weather were produced across parts of primarily North Texas. This event generated 6 tornadoes, 4 of which were in Johnson County. The strongest tornado was an EF-2. Additional swaths of damaging downburst winds were documented in Kaufman and Van Zandt counties.","168315":"Storms initiated along a cold front during the early evening hours of the 3rd, with several reports of large hail received across portions of western and central OK.","168515":"Thunderstorms developed over the mountains in northern Mexico and moved across the border into Texas. One of these storms produced large hail.","168601":"The remnants of a front across South Florida along with cold air aloft led to high amounts of instability which fostered the development of strong thunderstorms over interior portions of South Florida. Large hail up to 2 inches in diameter was the main impact."},"events":[{"begin":"2022-04-04T00:57Z","county":"Washita","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-04-04T00:57Z","endLat":35.21,"endLon":-99.11,"episode":168315,"id":1019012,"injuries":0,"lat":35.21,"location":"4.46 NW Rocky","lon":-99.11,"magnitude":1.18,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2022-04-04T01:25Z","county":"Caddo","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-04-04T01:25Z","endLat":35.4,"endLon":-98.58,"episode":168315,"id":1019014,"injuries":0,"lat":35.4,"location":"6.32 N Eakly","lon":-98.58,"magnitude":1.25,"narrative":"Time estimated from radar.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2022-04-04T03:07Z","county":"Comanche","damageCrops":"0.00K","dam